{
	"_comment": [
		"The allowlist of the route attribute gate: every controller method under lib/Controller that carries a route attribute, with its route and every attribute out of OCP\\AppFramework\\Http\\Attribute on the method and on its class.",
		"tests/Unit/RouteSecurityTest.php reads the controllers by reflection and requires an exact match. A new route, a changed attribute set, a changed verb or url and an entry without a method all turn the suite red.",
		"A change to a route or to its attributes is therefore entered here by hand and on purpose, and the entry is where a review answers the question why this route may do that.",
		"The format is the one tests/RouteSecurity/RouteProfiles.php produces: route is the short name of the route attribute, the verb and the url, followed by the canonical JSON of any further route argument; attributes are short names, sorted, with arguments as Name(key=value, ...).",
		"The textual gate backend/tests/test_php_trust_boundary.py stays beside this one: it checks the rejectForeignCaller call in the method bodies, which attributes cannot show."
	],
